bruits or thyromegaly. She also denies any edema.\n\nMs. Johnson reports that she has been working in a bakery this summer and has been enjoying it. She notes that it has been challenging to resist the temptation of the desserts.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fatigue.\nHENT: Denies thyromegaly or carotid bruits.\nMusculoskeletal: Denies back pain.\nNeurological: Denies headache.\nPsychiatric: Denies anxiety or depression.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nCV: Grade 2 systolic ejection murmur.\nRespiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.\nNeuro: Cranial: No bruits. Neurovascular: Normal.\nMusculoskeletal: No edema.\n\nRESULTS\n\nHemoglobin A1c: elevated.\nVital signs are normal.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nMs. Beverly Johnson is a 24-year-old female who presents for a yearly exam. Her history is significant for type 2 diabetes and hypertension.\n\nMs. Johnson\'s type 2 diabetes.\n- Medical Reasoning: The patient\'s hemoglobin A1c is elevated. She is currently on metformin twice daily. She has recently started working at a bakery and is struggling to resist the temptation of the desserts. I want to encourage her to reduce her snacking and additional sweets. I would like to see her in 2 months to check her blood sugar and see if we need to add another medication.\n- Medical Treatment: I am not going to change her medications at this time.\n\nMs. Johnson\'s hypertension.\n- Medical Reasoning: Her blood pressure is currently normal. I want her to continue her lisinopril 10 mg once a day.\n- Medical Treatment: Continue lisinopril 10 mg once a day.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nType 2 Diabetes and hypertension.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nMs. Beverly is a 24-year-old female who presents for her annual physical examination. She reports that she has been working at a bakery for the past few months and has been snacking on desserts