y ultrasound just to be sure that we are n\'t missing anything we wan na make sure there\'s no other causes like secondary causes that that\'s gon na cause some problems with your with your kidney okay\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] alright now for your third problem your kidney disease i do want to get some more labs some more blood work to make sure that you tolerate this regimen\n[patient] alright that sounds good\n[doctor] okay and if do you have any other questions for me\n[patient] i do n\'t think right now\n[doctor] okay well then i\'ll see you again in three months then kevin okay take care of yourself\n[patient] alright thanks document\n[doctor] alrighty bye\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nAcute on chronic heart failure.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nMr. Johnson is a pleasant 82-year-old male who presents for follow-up after an acute on chronic heart failure. He reports that he was doing well until he noticed that his ankles were swelling and he became short of breath. He called 911 and the paramedics placed him on a special mask. He was then evaluated at the Emergency Department where his blood pressure was noted to be 200/90 mmHg. He states that he has been trying to watch his diet as instructed. He has been taking his medications, but sometimes misses a dose or two. He is a big cheese lover and enjoys watching football and going to parties on the weekends. He loves pizza and chicken wings. He reports that he has been feeling well since his hospitalization. He has been urinating a lot and has been on a water pill through his IV. He has been taking his medications for his blood pressure as instructed. He has been checking his blood pressure at home and it has been good. He has been watching his diet and has not had any shortness of breath or chest pain. He has been sleeping well and has been taking an afternoon nap. He denies any chest pain. He reports that he has had a blood pressure cuff at home and has been checki